New: Portable::internal::batched::resolve_hanging_nodes() resolves the
hanging-node constraints of a batch of cells, whose values are stored cell
after cell, within a single team. Like the cell-wise
Portable::internal::resolve_hanging_nodes(), it uses one thread per
constrained line of degrees of freedom, now over all cells of the batch, and
a single team barrier per direction. The constraint masks of the cells of
the batch are passed as a Kokkos::View, which the caller sets up, e.g., as a
subview of the masks of all cells.
<br>
